WEBVTT

00:02.052 --> 00:04.552
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

00:06.690 --> 00:08.157
- Oh, hey, Alan.
- Hey, Herb.

00:08.158 --> 00:10.658
Jake, your dad's here.

00:11.561 --> 00:13.963
- So how's it going?
- All good.

00:13.964 --> 00:15.398
Good.

00:15.399 --> 00:16.966
- You?
- Good.

00:16.967 --> 00:19.467
Well, good.

00:20.370 --> 00:22.870
Yeah, good.

00:24.741 --> 00:27.241
Good.

00:30.347 --> 00:32.681
Oh, l, uh--
I see you've put in a new mailbox.

00:32.682 --> 00:34.884
Oh, yeah.
The old one was pretty shoddy.

00:34.885 --> 00:37.386
Whoever put it in
didn't anchor the pole correctly.

00:37.387 --> 00:39.855
That would be me.

00:39.856 --> 00:43.526
Oh, sorry. The mailman
was complaining about the wiggle.

00:43.527 --> 00:45.461
Herb, the mailman's a pothead.

00:45.462 --> 00:48.197
Yeah, I know.
I caught him eating my tomato plants.

00:48.198 --> 00:50.566
Anyway,
I decided to replace the whole thing.

00:50.567 --> 00:53.736
Yeah, I see it, uh--
It now says "The Melnicks."

00:53.737 --> 00:56.407
Well, I paid for the mailbox.

00:56.940 --> 00:59.074
I get my mail there.

00:59.075 --> 01:01.143
- My name's Melnick.
- Yeah, yeah, I get it.

01:01.144 --> 01:02.945
What's it say on your mailbox?

01:02.946 --> 01:05.446
Charlie Harper.

01:07.184 --> 01:09.385
Jake!

01:09.386 --> 01:12.555
No need to yell, he's in the bathroom.

01:12.556 --> 01:13.789
Big surprise, eh?

01:13.790 --> 01:17.259
He's either shoveling it in
or shooting it out. Ha, ha.

01:17.260 --> 01:19.261
Yeah, he's a regular
Play-Doh Fun Factory.

01:19.262 --> 01:20.429
[ALAN CHUCKLES]

01:20.430 --> 01:23.098
Just go make sure
he hasn't fallen asleep in there again.

01:23.099 --> 01:25.599
Yes, dear.

01:25.869 --> 01:28.103
So how's everything?

01:28.104 --> 01:31.874
Fine. Uh, listen, Alan, I've been thinking,
now that Jake's a teenager...

01:31.875 --> 01:34.543
...he'd benefit from spending
some more time with his dad.

01:34.544 --> 01:36.412
Oh. Oh, that would be great.

01:36.413 --> 01:39.281
Nothing would make me happier
than spending time with my son.

01:39.282 --> 01:41.050
- Good.
- Ha, ha.

01:41.051 --> 01:42.818
- Hey, Dad.
- Oh, hey, buddy.

01:42.819 --> 01:44.253
All finished in the bathroom?

01:44.254 --> 01:46.288
For now.
You should've seen the last one.

01:46.289 --> 01:49.119
It looked like a question mark.

01:56.800 --> 01:59.300
Go.

01:59.970 --> 02:03.239
Um, so, uh,
what are we talking about here?

02:03.240 --> 02:05.508
An extra day or two every other week?

02:05.509 --> 02:07.576
I was thinking more a solid three months.

02:07.577 --> 02:08.844
In a row?

02:08.845 --> 02:10.646
Alan, how many sons do you have?

02:10.647 --> 02:11.981
As many as you do.

02:11.982 --> 02:15.150
- Look, do you want your kid or not?
- Well, of course, but...

02:15.151 --> 02:18.287
Well, I'll have to clear it
with Charlie and...

02:18.288 --> 02:21.156
- And there is the financial issue.
- What financial issue?

02:21.157 --> 02:24.793
If he's living with me, I should get
a sizable break on the child support.

02:24.794 --> 02:30.464
- You're certainly entitled to your opinion.
- Well, thank you.

02:36.606 --> 02:39.106
Wait a minute.

02:40.043 --> 02:42.044
Three months in a row?

02:42.045 --> 02:44.380
- Oh, come on, it'll be fun.
- For who?

02:44.381 --> 02:47.483
All he does is eat, sleep,
and clog up the toilets.

02:47.484 --> 02:49.985
- Shh. Let's talk about this later.
- Oh, please.

02:49.986 --> 02:54.146
Chowderhead can't hear us.
Right, chowderhead?

02:54.658 --> 02:57.059
- See?
- Oh, just admit it.

02:57.060 --> 02:58.561
You love having him around.

02:58.562 --> 03:01.931
I love having him around
because I always know he's leaving.

03:01.932 --> 03:05.401
Don't take the leaving part
away from me, Alan.

03:05.402 --> 03:07.670
Let's just give it a chance,
see how it works.

03:07.671 --> 03:10.839
That's what Poland said
about the Germans.

03:10.840 --> 03:12.975
Been watching History Channel again?

03:12.976 --> 03:14.910
It's Nazi week.

03:14.911 --> 03:17.346
It's always Nazi week.

03:17.347 --> 03:20.583
Look, uh, tell you what, why don't I take
you and Jake out to dinner tonight?

03:20.584 --> 03:23.084
Can we get chili burgers?

03:59.155 --> 04:00.723
Wow, this is fun, huh?

04:00.724 --> 04:04.493
The three Harper boys sitting round
the campfire, putting on the feedbag.

04:04.494 --> 04:06.994
Yeah, bite me.

04:09.733 --> 04:12.233
So, numbnuts...

04:13.670 --> 04:16.105
...any thoughts why your mom
dumped you off on us?

04:16.106 --> 04:18.741
- Charlie.
- Oh, like you're not curious.

04:18.742 --> 04:20.776
No. No, I am not curious.

04:20.777 --> 04:23.879
She thought it'd be a good idea
to spend time with his father.

04:23.880 --> 04:29.590
And I'm trying to save girls
a long ride home on the freeway.

04:30.120 --> 04:32.287
So, what's your theory, Alfalfa?

04:32.288 --> 04:38.348
You're pretending to be considerate
so you can have sex with them.

04:39.629 --> 04:42.431
No, no.
I mean, about your mother and Herb.

04:42.432 --> 04:44.767
Oh, well, they are fighting a lot.

04:44.768 --> 04:48.135
- They're fighting?
- Yep, 31.

04:49.239 --> 04:51.106
Thirty-one?

04:51.107 --> 04:55.307
It's what you get
when you add 24 and seven.

04:57.280 --> 04:59.948
You know,
they're fighting all the time, 24/7.

04:59.949 --> 05:02.449
Thirty-one.

05:02.786 --> 05:05.654
- I'm not gonna make it three months, Alan.
- You'll be fine.

05:05.655 --> 05:08.757
- They're fighting in front of you?
- They don't think they are...

05:08.758 --> 05:13.028
...because when I wear the headphones,
I turn the music off.

05:13.029 --> 05:14.830
And you figured that out all by yourself?

05:14.831 --> 05:19.751
Hey, you may think I'm dumb,
but you overestimate me.

05:20.170 --> 05:22.438
My mistake.

05:22.439 --> 05:24.106
So, what are they arguing about?

05:24.107 --> 05:27.076
Well, she doesn't like his parents,
he doesn't like her spending...

05:27.077 --> 05:30.879
- ...and something about sex.
- What about sex?

05:30.880 --> 05:35.850
That's when I turn the music back on,
you sick freak.

05:38.421 --> 05:41.781
- Sorry.
- I mean, that's my mother.

05:41.891 --> 05:43.926
I said I'm sorry.

05:43.927 --> 05:47.463
Man, I'm not gonna make it three months.

05:47.464 --> 05:51.133
Oh, great.
Now he's got the moral high ground.

05:51.134 --> 05:52.634
[CHUCKLES]

05:52.635 --> 05:55.003
Forget about that.
The important thing is...

05:55.004 --> 05:57.506
...Judith and Herb
are having marital problems.

05:57.507 --> 05:59.475
[CHUCKLES]

05:59.476 --> 06:02.644
- Why does that make you happy?
- Well, it's not happiness exactly.

06:02.645 --> 06:04.346
It's just that all these years...

06:04.347 --> 06:09.818
...she's been blaming me
for the failure of our marriage and now--

06:09.819 --> 06:14.319
Yeah, I guess "happiness"
pretty much sums it up.

06:16.659 --> 06:19.261
Hey, what's this I hear
about little Lord Skidmark...

06:19.262 --> 06:22.252
...coming to live here full time?

06:22.665 --> 06:24.566
Oh, it's, uh, just for a few weeks.

06:24.567 --> 06:27.402
Uh, I'm sure if we all pull together,
you'll hardly notice.

06:27.403 --> 06:29.903
Yeah, pull this.

06:31.207 --> 06:32.407
Charlie.

06:32.408 --> 06:35.768
You and me gotta have a conversation.

06:37.280 --> 06:39.780
Nice talking to you.

06:39.916 --> 06:42.416
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

06:42.685 --> 06:43.886
Hey, Alan.

06:43.887 --> 06:46.755
- Oh, hey, Herb.
- Judith asked me to drop this off for Jake.

06:46.756 --> 06:47.956
Oh, here, let me help you.

06:47.957 --> 06:50.457
Thanks.

06:50.894 --> 06:56.865
So, what have you two lovebirds
got planned for the next few months?

06:56.866 --> 06:59.268
- Second honeymoon?
- No, not exactly.

06:59.269 --> 07:02.971
Oh. Hard to believe you're coming up
on your second anniversary.

07:02.972 --> 07:04.273
Yep, hard to believe.

07:04.274 --> 07:06.774
Two years. Ha, ha.

07:07.710 --> 07:10.345
Time flies when you're having fun, eh?

07:10.346 --> 07:12.846
I wouldn't know.

07:14.083 --> 07:16.351
- Hey, Herb.
- Hey, Charlie.

07:16.352 --> 07:21.302
You ask him about his marriage
going down the crapper?

07:23.293 --> 07:24.493
I was easing into it.

07:24.494 --> 07:26.994
So was l.

07:27.130 --> 07:28.463
What's the problem, Herb?

07:28.464 --> 07:31.166
Is it in the bedroom?
It usually starts in the bedroom.

07:31.167 --> 07:34.737
That's still my mother, you sick freak.

07:34.871 --> 07:38.574
We usually wait till he puts on headphones
before we discuss these things.

07:38.575 --> 07:41.510
Uh, gee, Herb, uh, something you should
know about the headphones--

07:41.511 --> 07:44.011
Shh, shh. Don't spoil it.

07:44.914 --> 07:46.648
So, what's the deal? Is it sex?

07:46.649 --> 07:48.917
No.

07:48.918 --> 07:51.620
Well, yeah, but it's no big deal.

07:51.621 --> 07:54.122
I mean, every marriage
has an ebb and flow to it.

07:54.123 --> 07:55.490
- Of course.
- Sure, sure.

07:55.491 --> 07:58.927
Right now,
Judith and I are kind of ebbing.

07:58.928 --> 08:00.796
A lot.

08:00.797 --> 08:03.297
Thirty-one.

08:04.734 --> 08:07.567
Right, 31.

08:08.338 --> 08:10.939
I don't know what's happening.
We can't communicate.

08:10.940 --> 08:14.576
She constantly finds fault with me.
I don't know what to do.

08:14.577 --> 08:16.011
I'll tell you what to do.

08:16.012 --> 08:20.082
What my testicle-challenged brother
should've done.

08:20.083 --> 08:23.619
She starts complaining, put your foot down.
Let her know who's in charge.

08:23.620 --> 08:26.488
And no matter what,
do not let her use sex as a weapon.

08:26.489 --> 08:30.058
Let her know if she won't satisfy
your needs, there's plenty of women.

08:30.059 --> 08:32.687
- Really?
- Why would I lie?

08:34.697 --> 08:37.566
Women like Judith respond to strength
and confidence.

08:37.567 --> 08:40.627
Not, well, that.

08:42.872 --> 08:44.873
Yeah, you make a compelling case.

08:44.874 --> 08:47.809
Damn right, I do.
Now go claim what's yours.

08:47.810 --> 08:50.880
I believe I will. Thanks, Charlie.

08:51.814 --> 08:54.314
I'm here for you, big guy.

08:55.485 --> 08:57.586
Why did you do that?

08:57.587 --> 09:00.087
I get bored.

09:06.596 --> 09:09.096
CHARLlE: Hey.
- Hey.

09:11.467 --> 09:14.269
- Why aren't you in school?
- I'm sick.

09:14.270 --> 09:16.571
Sick?

09:16.572 --> 09:20.342
Relax, I'm just faking
to get out of a Math test.

09:20.343 --> 09:23.437
Oh, okay, good. You scared me.

09:23.746 --> 09:25.180
What's with the staple gun?

09:25.181 --> 09:28.431
Oh, the sole is coming off my shoe.

09:29.319 --> 09:31.019
Ah.

09:31.020 --> 09:34.140
You might wanna take it off first.

09:34.524 --> 09:37.024
Good call.

09:42.799 --> 09:43.966
Morning.

09:43.967 --> 09:45.133
[STAPLE GUN CLlCKS]

09:45.134 --> 09:46.368
It's none of my business...

09:46.369 --> 09:50.806
...but that's one kid that can't afford
to miss a single day at school.

09:50.807 --> 09:53.307
[STAPLE GUN CLlCKS]

09:53.343 --> 09:56.545
Yeah, like school's gonna make
a difference.

09:56.546 --> 09:57.813
[STAPLE GUN CLlCKS]

09:57.814 --> 10:00.314
JAKE:
Ow! Crap!

10:00.783 --> 10:03.877
I stapled my fingers together.

10:05.054 --> 10:07.554
You got a point.

10:12.729 --> 10:14.596
Come on, honey, blow.

10:14.597 --> 10:17.097
[BLOWS NOSE]

10:21.437 --> 10:24.206
- What's he got?
- A cold, I think.

10:24.207 --> 10:27.007
Why didn't you leave him home?

10:27.176 --> 10:29.311
That way, we all don't get sick.

10:29.312 --> 10:31.480
[COUGHS]

10:31.481 --> 10:36.485
That's why you always take your shoes
to a qualified, professional cobbler.

10:36.486 --> 10:39.766
You know what's good? Apple cobbler.

10:39.856 --> 10:41.690
What's the damage, doc?

10:41.691 --> 10:43.825
Will he play the violin again?

10:43.826 --> 10:46.795
He'll be fine. You might wanna
keep him away from staple guns.

10:46.796 --> 10:49.331
- Right.
- Also nail guns, glue guns.

10:49.332 --> 10:52.367
Pretty much anything with "gun" in it.

10:52.368 --> 10:54.868
Got it. Thanks, Herb.

10:55.738 --> 10:58.006
Hey, uh, Charlie, can I talk to you for a sec?

10:58.007 --> 11:00.308
- You wait for me in the car.
- Give me the keys.

11:00.309 --> 11:02.210
I'm not giving you the keys.

11:02.211 --> 11:05.514
- Then how am I gonna wait in the car?
- Wait by the car.

11:05.515 --> 11:08.650
I don't have sunscreen on.
I'm very fair-skinned.

11:08.651 --> 11:11.151
Then wait under the car.

11:14.457 --> 11:15.657
What's up?

11:15.658 --> 11:18.894
Well, uh, you remember that advice
you gave me about Judith?

11:18.895 --> 11:23.732
Oh, gee, Herb, that wasn't so much advice
as, you know, social satire.

11:23.733 --> 11:25.200
Well, it worked out great.

11:25.201 --> 11:28.303
Really?
She bought that king-of-the-castle crap?

11:28.304 --> 11:31.039
No, no. She kicked my ass out.

11:31.040 --> 11:35.343
The thing is, talking to you and seeing how
you live I'm convinced I'm better off single.

11:35.344 --> 11:36.945
- ls that so?
- Oh, yeah.

11:36.946 --> 11:42.317
I mean, uh, why chew on one chicken wing
when you can eat from the whole bucket?

11:42.318 --> 11:45.353
Just so there's no confusion,
chicken wings are...?

11:45.354 --> 11:49.357
Women, Charlie.
I was offering up a metaphor.

11:49.358 --> 11:52.994
And you went with wings
rather than breasts and thighs?

11:52.995 --> 11:55.495
Oh, that is better.

11:55.932 --> 11:57.232
Anyway, I was thinking, uh...

11:57.233 --> 12:02.070
...maybe you and I could go out some time
and, uh, get a party pack.

12:02.071 --> 12:05.874
Sex with strange women.
Uh, I was extending the metaphor.

12:05.875 --> 12:08.110
Of course. Sure, let's do that sometime.

12:08.111 --> 12:10.378
Thanks again for sewing up the kid.

12:10.379 --> 12:12.414
So, uh, what color you like?

12:12.415 --> 12:14.915
Excuse me?

12:15.952 --> 12:20.552
Oh, I was thinking Asian
but I'll take the green.

12:29.198 --> 12:31.032
- Hey, Dad.
- Oh, hey.

12:31.033 --> 12:32.534
- How are you feeling?
- Fine.

12:32.535 --> 12:35.035
Throat's not sore anymore?

12:35.071 --> 12:37.571
Ahem. Oh, yeah, a little.

12:37.607 --> 12:39.207
[COUGHS]

12:39.208 --> 12:44.878
- What happened to your fingers?
- Oh, I stapled them together.

12:45.381 --> 12:47.616
Ah.

12:47.617 --> 12:49.518
Hey, hey.

12:49.519 --> 12:52.689
We do not leave our shoes on the--

12:57.527 --> 13:00.027
What the hell?

13:02.632 --> 13:05.901
We need to get rid of the staple gun.

13:05.902 --> 13:11.832
Alan, staple guns don't staple shoes
to coffee tables, idiots do.

13:12.875 --> 13:15.177
Why are you taking your temperature?

13:15.178 --> 13:18.813
I think some little snot locker
gave me smallpox.

13:18.814 --> 13:21.314
[PHONE RlNGlNG]

13:22.084 --> 13:24.746
Oh, man. Leave me alone.

13:25.821 --> 13:29.090
Is that Mom? You think maybe
I might wanna talk to her?

13:29.091 --> 13:32.994
- Do you?
- Of course not, it's the principle.

13:32.995 --> 13:34.796
Well, that wasn't Mom. It was Herb.

13:34.797 --> 13:36.798
Why is Herb calling?

13:36.799 --> 13:40.035
Since Judith threw him out,
he wants me to help him pick up women.

13:40.036 --> 13:43.138
Wait, back up, back up, back up,
back up, back up, back up.

13:43.139 --> 13:46.007
Wait, Judith threw Herb out? When?

13:46.008 --> 13:49.077
I don't know.
Apparently, about a week ago.

13:49.078 --> 13:50.312
Oh, my God.

13:50.313 --> 13:52.681
That's terrible.

13:52.682 --> 13:55.182
Judith must be devastated.

14:00.590 --> 14:02.257
- Alan?
- Yeah?

14:02.258 --> 14:05.508
You got a little evil on your face.

14:06.395 --> 14:08.895
- Other side.
- Oh.

14:14.070 --> 14:16.766
Oh, Judith, that's terrible.

14:16.939 --> 14:19.567
You must be devastated.

14:21.377 --> 14:22.877
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

14:22.878 --> 14:25.438
You must be devastated.

14:26.816 --> 14:27.983
Oh.

14:27.984 --> 14:30.151
- What're you doing here?
- Oh, sorry to bother you.

14:30.152 --> 14:33.555
Apparently, uh, Jake left
his Social Studies book, so here I am.

14:33.556 --> 14:35.957
I think I saw it in the bathroom.

14:35.958 --> 14:38.918
Why? Was he out of toilet paper?

14:41.964 --> 14:44.332
Wouldn't it be great
if he could learn that way?

14:44.333 --> 14:47.302
You know, uh, "ass-mosis." Heh.

14:48.571 --> 14:51.071
JUDlTH: What?
- Nothing.

14:51.841 --> 14:53.742
Is Herb around?

14:53.743 --> 14:54.909
Uh, no.

14:54.910 --> 14:58.141
- Oh, oh, too bad.
- Why?

14:58.748 --> 15:02.050
Oh, no reason.
I just, uh, enjoy seeing the big galoot.

15:02.051 --> 15:04.552
Well, the galoot is not here.

15:04.553 --> 15:07.053
Oh. Well, uh...

15:07.623 --> 15:10.583
- Tell him I said hi.
- I will.

15:14.330 --> 15:15.797
[JUDlTH SOBBlNG]

15:15.798 --> 15:18.133
Herb moved out.

15:18.134 --> 15:21.262
Our marriage is over.

15:22.004 --> 15:24.544
Oh, Judith, that's terrible.

15:25.041 --> 15:27.541
[SOBBlNG CONTlNUES]

15:29.278 --> 15:31.940
You must be devastated.

15:42.591 --> 15:44.926
What exactly do you have in mind?

15:44.927 --> 15:47.725
- Give me your hand.
- Okay.

15:47.897 --> 15:50.397
Do I feel warm to you?

15:50.900 --> 15:52.534
HERB:
Dude.

15:52.535 --> 15:54.035
Aw, crap.

15:54.036 --> 15:59.986
So, uh, you fishing here,
or can I throw my bobber in the water?

16:00.576 --> 16:03.076
Bye.

16:05.114 --> 16:08.717
- How'd you know I was here?
- I tried calling. Your phone must be broken.

16:08.718 --> 16:10.952
I went by your house.
Jake said you went out.

16:10.953 --> 16:14.022
All I had to do was punch "liquor"
into the in-dash navigation.

16:14.023 --> 16:16.643
And three stops later, voilà.

16:16.926 --> 16:18.927
So, uh, they biting tonight?

16:18.928 --> 16:22.030
Okay, okay. First of all,
can we stop with the fish talk?

16:22.031 --> 16:25.033
Believe me,
it's not gonna lead any place good.

16:25.034 --> 16:26.534
Back to the chickens?

16:26.535 --> 16:28.603
If we must.

16:28.604 --> 16:30.472
I'll have what he's having.

16:30.473 --> 16:33.575
I'm having a tall pain in the ass.

16:33.576 --> 16:37.066
Sounds good. Does that have rum in it?

16:38.147 --> 16:41.683
How did this happen?
How did I blow another marriage?

16:41.684 --> 16:43.618
Oh, sweetie, you can't blame yourself.

16:43.619 --> 16:46.855
Although you are
the common denominator.

16:46.856 --> 16:50.759
Alan, I'm 40 years old.
How am I ever gonna start over again?

16:50.760 --> 16:54.960
I know, I know.
And soon you're gonna be 41.

16:55.531 --> 16:59.033
Do you have any idea what it's like
to date when all the men your age...

16:59.034 --> 17:01.803
...are only interested
in 25-year-old hard bodies?

17:01.804 --> 17:04.304
Well, you can't blame us.

17:05.841 --> 17:08.443
Well, of course you can't compete
hard body to hard body...

17:08.444 --> 17:11.579
...but you're still a very desirable woman.

